{"kind":"request","text":"Add a harness case that places a checkpoint near the head of a deep sequence.","body":{"conditions":"Measurement gap found while evidencing the envelopes at main adda28c8. Every checkpoint case in the gitseq.performance/v1 contract computes its checkpoint depth as sample depth minus tail, and all six cases resolve to depth 257, so no fixture has ever contained a checkpoint sitting near the head of a deep sequence. The consequence is that restart from a checkpoint at FIRST-PRODUCTION depth cannot be measured: tail verification cost is depth-independent and carries, but the cost of loading and authenticating a 500,000-record checkpoint is unmeasured, which is why docs/reference/performance.md records FIRST-PRODUCTION cold restart as not established rather than as a pass. This is the one envelope target on that page that no measurement can currently decide. Satisfied when the contract carries at least one checkpoint case whose checkpoint sits within the refresh cadence of the head at 50,000 and at 500,000 records, the harness prepares such fixtures, and a restart measurement at both depths is reported so the FIRST-PRODUCTION restart verdict can be settled as a pass or a miss on evidence.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}